schway-screen 1
screen resumed-review-details
title Resumed review details
description F2 explains that previous turn details are unavailable and names the current workspace and branch.
variant dark-120
size 120x30
cursor 1 1 hidden
== text
 ⚡ schway  ***/home/demo on main

  Review · current changes

  Current working tree  │ Current changes details
  › clamp.ts   unstaged │ Previous turn details unavailable
    notes.md  untracked │ No live turn record is held, so this review shows the current working tree instead. Schway
                        │ keeps file-tool counts, snapshots, elapsed time and command exits only in memory for the
                        │ latest turn of this run. After restart, resume or a session or branch switch it cannot show
                        │ what an earlier turn changed, and it does not rebuild that from saved conversation text.
                        │
                        │ Workspace: ***/home/demo
                        │ Branch: main
                        │
                        │ Review scope:
                        │ Current working tree: paths Git reports as staged, unstaged or untracked when review opens
                        │ or Ctrl+R reloads. They can include edits from earlier turns, other tools and people, and
                        │ omit changes that were committed or reverted. The state beside each path is current Git
                        │ state, not authorship.
                        │ Current diff is read from Git when review opens, when you select a file and when Ctrl+R
                        │ reloads. It does not update live and is never the exact patch of a resumed turn.
                        │ Unstaged compares the index with the worktree. Staged compares HEAD, or the empty tree
                        │ before the first commit, with the index. Untracked shows the current file.


